# Node
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

# Build and check output. The checker compiles each sample into a temporary
# directory outside the repository, but a stray local run should not be
# committable either.
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Credentials and secrets. Nothing in these notes needs any, which is exactly
# when an accidental commit happens.
#
# BOTH glob forms, because neither implies the other. `.env*` is a prefix glob:
# it catches .env, .env.local and .envrc, the last of which direnv uses and
# people put exported secrets in. `*.env` is a suffix glob, for names like
# audit.env or production.env. An earlier version of this file listed `.env.*`
# instead of `.env*`, and the dot is not cosmetic: `.env.*` requires a second
# dot, so it cannot match .envrc at all.
#
# The negation is the other half. `.env*` also matches .env.example, which is
# the one file in this family you are supposed to commit, so it is re-included
# explicitly. Order matters: the negation has to come after the pattern it
# undoes, since the last matching rule wins.
.env*
*.env
!.env.example
secrets/
credentials*
*.pem
*.key

# Logs, databases, editor and OS noise. Both sqlite spellings: the extension is
# a convention rather than a rule, and .sqlite3 is at least as common as .sqlite.
*.log
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
__pycache__/
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
